hardware_manager: suspend_action = none -- ignore Android's suspend request

When Android's display sleeps it asks the host to suspend; the only actions
were "stop" (tear the session down) and anything else = freeze the whole
container, both of which stop audio. "none" keeps the container running, so
Android can turn its display off -- no composition, an idle GPU -- while a
music app keeps playing.

--- a/tools/services/hardware_manager.py	2026-10-07 19:08:50.517764713 +0900
+++ b/tools/services/hardware_manager.py	2026-10-07 19:08:50.558488828 +0900
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
         cfg = tools.config.load(args)
         if cfg["waydroid"]["suspend_action"] == "stop":
             tools.actions.session_manager.stop(args)
+        elif cfg["waydroid"]["suspend_action"] == "none":
+            # Ignore Android's request: the container keeps running, so audio
+            # keeps playing with the display off.
+            return
         else:
             tools.actions.container_manager.freeze(args)
 
